  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "How to read it",
   "value": "The chart is drawn against POSITIONS. No name appears on it. Who holds each position is in the legend at the end, so when somebody leaves or moves, one legend row changes and the drawing itself stands.\n\nThat is the failure of the chart dated 01.04.2022: it was drawn around eight names, so as those people moved the whole drawing went stale rather than one line of it. Four years on it still had Stores and Dispatch under each other's in-charge.\n\nThe same structure follows as a list, because a drawing cannot be searched and because a reporting line is worth stating as well as drawing. Both come from the job descriptions, which are the controlled documents that state them.",
   "lines": 0
  },
